selftext:
 Age: 26 Weight: 125lbs Height: 5'9 Gender: Male Medications: None currently but history below Smoking status: Never Medical Issues: Previous: Lyme disease, chronic dehydration that lead to Syncope. Current: Major Depression' Race: White Location: Maryland Duration: 18 years, but only seeking treatment for 3 years 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

My psychiatrist told me last appointment that he doesn't think he can help me anymore. Clinically diagnosed major depression. Been on nearly every ssri, some snri, Wellbutrin, vit d supplement, mood stabilizers, and an anti-psychotic to try to help manage the symptoms with no positive results. This now makes 1 family doctor, 1 psychiatrist, and 3 therapists that have given up on treating me.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

I honestly dont know what else is left. the doctor wanted to try tms and esketamine but they werent covered and too expensive as last options. I really feel like im not living a life worth living and idk what else i can do. help?

